{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"641","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Little Artem and Random Variable"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little Artyom decided to study probability theory. He found a book with a lot of nice exercises and now wants you to help him with one of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider two dices. When thrown each dice shows some integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" inclusive. For each dice the probability of each outcome is given (of course, their sum is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and different dices may have different probability distributions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We throw both dices simultaneously and then calculate values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"max(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to the outcome of the first dice, while "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to the outcome of the second dice. You don't know the probability distributions for particular values on each dice, but you know the probability distributions for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"max(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":". That is, for each "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" you know the probability that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"max(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" would be equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the probability that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" would be equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":". Find any valid probability distribution for values on the dices. It's guaranteed that the input data is consistent, that is, at least one solution exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First line contains the integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of different values for both dices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Second line contains an array consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" real values with up to 8 digits after the decimal point  — probability distribution for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"max(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":", the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of these values equals to the probability that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"max(a, b) = i"},{"kind":"text","text":". It's guaranteed that the sum of these values for one dice is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The third line contains the description of the distribution "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the same format."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output two descriptions of the probability distribution for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the first line and for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the second line. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer will be considered correct if each value of max("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a, b"},{"kind":"text","text":") and min("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a, b"},{"kind":"text","text":") probability distribution values does not differ by more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":" from ones given in input. Also, probabilities should be non-negative and their sums should differ from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" by no more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n0.25 0.75\n0.75 0.25\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.5 0.5 \n0.5 0.5 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n0.125 0.25 0.625\n0.625 0.25 0.125\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.25 0.25 0.5 \n0.5 0.25 0.25 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"641D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/641/problem/D"}